  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Second Program for Strengthening Governance for Enabling Service Delivery and Public Investment in Kenya</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed Additional Financing (AF) will strengthen priority reforms across core public financial management (PFM) functions.  Specifically, it will support strengthening domestic resource mobilization and compliance; enhancing PFM and expenditure efficiency; deepening digitalization of government systems and data governance; improving transparency and accountability mechanisms; and reinforcing institutional capacity for policy design and implementation. Building on these priorities, the AF will be anchored in a set of indicative disbursement-linked indicators (DLIs) that translate reforms into measurable, time-bound results. These will include reducing the value-added tax (VAT) and personal income tax (PIT) compliance gaps; increasing fiscal savings and reducing pending bills; improving budget reliability; strengthening external scrutiny and audit of public finances; and promoting the anti-corruption and conflict-of-interest prevention agendas.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To enhance public sector efficiency, accountability, and transparency through improving revenue systems, spending controls, public sector effectiveness, and oversight.</narrative>
  </description>
